        "original_id": "b7df59d6-cce1-5e74-9cdf-1462aefec25f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Gilgit-Baltistan\n- Systems: Karakoram, Hispar Muztagh, Yengisogat\n- Topics: Distaghil Sar, The Crown\n\nFacts:\n- Distaghil Sar is the highest mountain in the Hispar Muztagh subrange of the Karakoram mountain range in Gilgit-Baltistan.\n- Distaghil Sar has an approximately 3 km-long summit ridge above 7400 m with three distinct summits: the northwest summit at 7885 m, the central summit at 7760 m, and the southeast summit at 7696 m or 7535 m.\n- The Crown has an elevation of 7295 m and is the highest peak in the Yengisogat subrange of the Karakoram.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "73474061-7033-58ec-92fe-71ceb610dd17",
        "text": "Page: Distaghil Sar. Sentence: Disteghil Sar or Distaghil Sar (Urdu: ‎ ) is the highest mountain in the Hispar Muztagh, a subrange of the Karakoram mountain range, in Gilgit-Baltistan.\nPage: Distaghil Sar. Sentence: The mountain has an about 3 km long top ridge above 7400m with three distinct summits: (north)west 7885m, central 7760 m, and (south)east 7696m or 7535m ().\nPage: The Crown (mountain). Sentence: Its summit has an elevation of 7295 m and it is the highest peak in the Yengisogat subrange of the Karakoram.",
